    "raw_reply": "Looking at the code, I need to analyze data dependences between iterations for each of the three loops.\n\n**Loop at line 9** (copying `a` to `old_a`):\n```cpp\nfor (int i = 0; i < LEN_1D; ++i) {\n    old_a[i] = a[i];\n}\n```\nEach iteration i writes to `old_a[i]` and reads from `a[i]`. Different iterations access different array indices, so there are no cross-iteration dependences.\n\n**Loop at line 12** (main computation):\n```cpp\nfor (int i = 0; i < LEN_1D-1; ++i) {\n    a[i] = b[i] + c[i] * d[i];           // Line 13\n    b[i] = c[i] + b[i];                   // Line 14\n    a[i+1] = b[i] + old_a[i+1] * d[i];   // Line 15\n}\n```\nIn iteration i: writes to `a[i]`, `b[i]`, and `a[i+1]` (lines 13, 14, 15)\nIn iteration i+1: writes to `a[i+1]` (line 13), `b[i+1]` (line 14), and `a[i+2]` (line 15)\n\nBoth iteration i and i+1 write to `a[i+1]` \u2014 iteration i on line 15 and iteration i+1 on line 13. This is a WAW dependence.\n\n**Loop at line 8** (outer loop):\nBetween iterations nl and nl+1:\n- Iteration nl writes to: `a[0..LEN_1D-1]` (lines 13, 15), `b[0..LEN_1D-2]` (line 14), `old_a[0..LEN_1D-1]` (line 10)\n- Iteration nl+1 reads from: `a[0..LEN_1D-1]` (line 10), `b[0..LEN_1D-2]` (lines 13, 14, 15), `old_a[1..LEN_1D-1]` (line 15)\n- Iteration nl reads from: `a[0..LEN_1D-1]` (line 10), `b[0..LEN_1D-2]` (lines 13, 14, 15), `old_a[1..LEN_1D-1]` (line 15)\n- Iteration nl+1 writes to: same as iteration nl\n\nThis creates RAW, WAW, and WAR dependences:\n\nLOOP 9 NONE\nLOOP 12 WAW a 15 13\nLOOP 8 RAW a 15 10\nLOOP 8 RAW b 14 13\nLOOP 8 RAW old_a 10 15\nLOOP 8 WAW a 15 13\nLOOP 8 WAR a 13 10\nLOOP 8 WAR b 14 13\nLOOP 8 WAR old_a 10 15",
